    {"attribute": "book_atomic_habits_guidelines", "value": "[\"The concept of atomic habits refers to the idea that small, incremental changes in our habits can lead to significant improvements in our lives.\", \"To make it easier to start a new habit, it is important to make the habit obvious.\", \"To make it easier to perform a new habit, it is important to make the habit attractive.\", \"To make it easier to perform a new habit, it is important to make the habit easy.\", \"To make it easier to persevere with a new habit, it is important to make the habit satisfying.\", \"Our habits are closely tied to our identity and the type of person we believe ourselves to be.\", \"Willpower is a limited resource that can be depleted through use.\", \"This can be done through the process of substitution, in which a new habit is created to replace the old one.\", \"To stick with good habits, it is important to focus on building a system of good habits rather than relying on motivation alone.\", \"To help others create good habits, it is important to make the new habit obvious, attractive, easy, and satisfying for them.\"]"}
]

